# Feature Requirements

## Version: 1.0.0
Last Updated: 2026-02-10

---

## Feature: Badge Component
Priority: High
Status: In Progress

### Overview
A display-only badge component for labels, status, and counts. Supports default/disabled states, six colors, three sizes, three radius options, five variants (Solid, Bordered, Light, Shadow, Dot), and start/end content slots. Uses the project's design token system. Visual reference: Variants (Solid, Bordered, Light, Shadow, Dot) and Radius (Full, Medium, Small) screenshots.

### Requirements

#### 1. Default
- Render as `<span>` (non-interactive)
- Base BEM class: `.aceui-badge`
- Defaults: variant `solid`, color `primary`, size `medium`, radius `full`
- Use design tokens from `design-tokens.css`

#### 2. Disabled State
- Support `isDisabled` prop (boolean)
- Modifier: `.aceui-badge--disabled`
- Opacity: `var(--aceui-disabled-opacity)`
- Set `aria-disabled="true"` when disabled
- Cursor / pointer-events as needed for display-only

#### 3. Colors
Support `color` prop with six values; BEM `.aceui-badge--color-{name}`. Use same token pattern as Button:
- **default**, **primary**, **secondary**, **success**, **warning**, **danger**
- Each: base `--aceui-color-{name}-500`, foreground `--aceui-color-{name}-foreground`; shades 50–900 for variants (e.g. light = color-50 bg, color-500 text)

#### 4. Size
- **small**: `.aceui-badge--small` — max-height 24px, font-size/line-height/padding from tokens (small)
- **medium** (default): `.aceui-badge--medium` — max-height 28px
- **large**: `.aceui-badge--large` — max-height 32px

#### 5. Radius
- **full**: `.aceui-badge--radius-full` — border-radius 9999px (pill)
- **medium**: `.aceui-badge--radius-medium` — `var(--aceui-radius-medium)`
- **small**: `.aceui-badge--radius-small` — `var(--aceui-radius-small)`

#### 6. Variants
- **Solid**: `.aceui-badge--solid` — Filled background (color-500), foreground text
- **Bordered**: `.aceui-badge--bordered` — Transparent bg, border + text from color
- **Light**: `.aceui-badge--light` — Light bg (color-50), text from color (500)
- **Shadow**: `.aceui-badge--shadow` — Like Solid + box-shadow using `--aceui-badge-shadow-opacity` and color
- **Dot**: `.aceui-badge--dot` — Same base style as solid/light etc. + `.aceui-badge__dot` before label (small circle, color from current semantic token)

#### 7. Start / End Content
- `startContent`, `endContent` (ReactNode)
- Render in `.aceui-badge__start` and `.aceui-badge__end`
- Gap from spacing tokens
- When variant is Dot: render dot then optional startContent then children then endContent

### BEM Class Structure
- Block: `.aceui-badge`
- Elements: `.aceui-badge__dot`, `.aceui-badge__start`, `.aceui-badge__content`, `.aceui-badge__end`
- Modifiers: `.aceui-badge--{variant}`, `.aceui-badge--color-{color}`, `.aceui-badge--small|medium|large`, `.aceui-badge--radius-{radius}`, `.aceui-badge--disabled`

### Component API
```typescript
interface BadgeProps {
  children?: React.ReactNode;
  variant?: 'solid' | 'bordered' | 'light' | 'shadow' | 'dot';
  color?: 'default' | 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger';
  size?: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
  radius?: 'full' | 'medium' | 'small';
  isDisabled?: boolean;
  startContent?: React.ReactNode;
  endContent?: React.ReactNode;
  ariaLabel?: string;
  className?: string;
  testId?: string;
}
```
